// Real-agent BasicSummon (the `find_familiar.ron` shape), scaled to two
// fighters -- "persist while you concentrate, striking at foes you direct
// them against" needs real agency, same reasoning as `conjure_animals.ron`
// but constructs instead of beasts. `duration` matches the spell's own
// `Concentration(60)`. `body: Golem(ClayGolem)` stands in for "mechanical
// figures" at combat scale, distinct from the tiny `Mogwai` used by the
// non-combat homunculus spells in this batch. The sheet's Force
// `damage_type` and `Cone 18` `aoe` are flavor-only here: `BasicSummon` has
// no damage/AoE field of its own -- any damage this construct deals comes
// from its own NPC loadout/stats, not this ability, the same gap every other
// summon spell in this batch that lists a `damage_type` already has (none
// of them mechanically express it either). The compendium entry's own `aoe`
// is left `None` rather than `Some(Cone(18.0))` for the same reason -- the
// spellbook tooltip reads straight off that field, and advertising a cone
// shape `BasicSummon` never actually produces would mislead the player.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 1.0,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 2,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 4.0),
        body: Golem((species: ClayGolem, body_type: Male)),
        scale: None,
        has_health: true,
        use_npc_name: true,
        loadout_config: None,
        skillset_config: None,
        duration: Some((secs: 60, nanos: 0)),
    ),
)
